{"type":"message","id":"3a298466","parentId":"499ddae0","timestamp":"2026-10-20T02:35:39.913Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the bug in `to_cents` in `ledger/currency.py`. `tests/test_totals.py` and the rest of the suite now pass (5 tests).\n\n**Cause:** `to_cents` used `int(amount * 100)`, which cuts off the decimals instead of rounding. Because of how floats are stored, `19.99 * 100` comes out as `1998.9999…`, so it was converted to 1998 cents instead of 1999.\n\n**Fix:** it now uses `round(amount * 100)`, so it rounds to the nearest cent. `to_cents` is only called from `Line.cents`, so the fix covers every caller.\n\nOne limit: Python's `round` sends exact halves to the nearest even number. That only matters for prices with half a cent in them (like 1.005), which don't seem to occur here. Prices are still passed around as floats; switching to `Decimal` would remove the issue for good, but that's a bigger change."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"vertex-anthropic","model":"claude-opus-5-5","usage":{"input":2,"output":306,"cacheRead":30274,"cacheWrite":2302,"totalTokens":32884,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0},"cttl":{"ephemeral5m":2302}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1792463736097,"responseId":"msg_vrtx_011CgCi7kwX6te2DCfgFsvSj","duration":3814.898319,"ttft":3787.488265,"contextSnapshot":{"promptTokens":32578,"nonMessageTokens":15621}}}
